== Method chosen by the tester (no steps in the DB)
"Link flap at supported speed": every live x230 link runs at the only speed its pluggable/partner pair negotiates here,
1000 Mb/s full duplex (autonegotiated). Each link is flapped 3 times, two ways, and its status checked after every flap:
  Step A: local admin flap on the x230 (shutdown / no shutdown) on port1.0.5, 1.0.4, 1.0.3, 1.0.2;
  Step B: remote flap -- the partner port is shut and re-enabled on the IE520 stack (port1.0.17, 1.0.3, 1.0.2), so the
          x230 sees a real loss of link and its recovery; checked from the x230's log and status.
  Pass criteria: each flap gives exactly one Port down + one Port up notification on the x230, the port returns to
  "connected a-full a-1000" (the speed/duplex it had before), its VLAN is unchanged and the LLDP neighbour returns.
  port1.0.5's partner is tb470 eth3 (a host NIC); a remote flap of it needs root (ip link) -> local flap only.
  port1.0.1 (AT-SPTXa to AR4050S port1.0.2, admin-shut on the 4050) has no link -> not flapped here (T47208 brings it up).

